-- title:
--   Descent of T-points along B → B ⊗ 𝒪̂^{nr}
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$ and a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ that is a discrete valuation ring with irreducible element $\pi$, $\pi$-adically complete, whose residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements and in which $(r) = (\pi)$. Let $Onr$ be a characteristic-zero domain over $\mathcal O$, with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, such that $Onr$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every element of $Onr$ satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo it, every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo it, and $Fr(x) \equiv x^r$ modulo it for all $x$. Let $m > 0$ and let $S$ be the equalizer of $Fr^m$ and the identity, i.e. the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $Fr^m$-fixed elements of $Onr$; let $FrS$ be an $S$-algebra automorphism of $Onr$ with $FrS(x) = Fr^m(x)$ for all $x$. Let $B$ be a commutative ring that is simultaneously an $\mathcal O$-algebra and an $S$-algebra, compatibly, with the image of $\pi$ in $B$ nilpotent. Then for every scheme $T$ and every morphism $f \colon \operatorname{Spec}(B \otimes_S Onr) \to T$ invariant under $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathrm{id}_B \otimes FrS$, in the sense that $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathrm{id}_B \otimes FrS)$ followed by $f$ equals $f$, there exists $g \colon \operatorname{Spec} B \to T$ such that $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusion $B \to B \otimes_S Onr$ followed by $g$ equals $f$.
--
--   This is the existence half of scalar descent for $T$-valued points along the unramified base change $B \to B \otimes_S Onr$: a morphism to an arbitrary scheme invariant under the geometric Frobenius twist descends to $\operatorname{Spec} B$. It is combined with the corresponding uniqueness statement in [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.existsUnique_specMap_includeLeft_comp_eq_of_specMap_frobenius_comp_eq`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.existsUnique_specMap_includeLeft_comp_eq_of_specMap_frobenius_comp_eq), and serves the comparison of Deligne data over $\pi$-nilpotent bases in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation.
